{{ define "page:main" }}
<h1>{{ .Page.Title }}</h1>
<subtitle>{{ .Page.PublishedDate }}</subtitle>

<ol>
  <li>
    I believe that my primary goal when leading a team is to optimise for my
    team's learning. If I have optimised for my team's learning, anything else
    (delivering a product) is a side effect.
  </li>
  <li>
    Regular interactions with my team serve as the vehicle for driving the
    growth of the engineers under my care. These regular interactions happen in
    weekly 1:1s, code reviews, architectural discussions, watercooler
    conversations and whatnot.
  </li>
  <li>
    The foundation for growth of the engineers under my care is psychological
    safety. Psychological safety is a result of making sure that an engineer has
    their personal life sorted, a comfortable working environment, feels
    included in the team, has some downtime for reflection, and an avenue to
    vent their frustrations.
  </li>
  <li>
    The only thing I can ask of an engineer under my care is that they strive to
    do good work.
  </li>
  <li>
    The marker for growth in an engineer is an increase in their scope of work.
    For example, an engineer starts out working on a small component in a
    service and eventually graduates to working on an entire module in a
    service.
  </li>
  <li>It is very important that the team celebrates victories often.</li>
  <li>
    A good whiteboard and a set of nice whiteboard markers is one of the best
    investments you can make for a team.
  </li>
</ol>
{{ end }}
